.Dd $Mdocdate: October 4 2026 $
.Dt BTCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm btctl
.Nd control the Bluetooth daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
program controls the
.Xr btd 8
daemon.
Commands may be abbreviated.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s Ar socket
Use
.Ar socket
instead of the default
.Pa /dev/btd.sock .
.El
.Pp
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm log brief
Disable verbose debug logging.
.It Cm log verbose
Enable verbose debug logging.
.It Cm reload
Reload the configuration file.
.It Cm show Op Cm devices
Show the configured devices, their state, the battery level of a
connected keyboard or mouse that reports one and, while pairing a
keyboard, the passkey to type on it.
.It Cm show bonds
Show the stored bonds, without the keys.
.It Cm show controller
Show the controller: addresses, versions, firmware and buffers.
.It Cm unpair Ar address
Remove the bonds stored for
.Ar address
and drop its link, so that the device is paired again when it is
next found.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/btd.sockXX" -compact
.It Pa /dev/btd.sock
.Ux Ns -domain
socket used for communication with
.Xr btd 8 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr btd.conf 5 ,
.Xr btd 8
